==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|iniquite|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|iniquité|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|iniquitas|lang=la}}, from {{term|iniquus|lang=la||unjust, harmful}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ɪnˈɪk.wɪ.ti/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|iniquities}}

# [[deviation|Deviation]] from what is right; [[wickedness]], [[gross]] [[injustice]].
#* '''1994''', [[w:Pulp Fiction (film)#Jules.27s_Bible_passage|Jules, ''Pulp Fiction'']],
#*: The path of the righteous man is beset on all sides by the '''iniquities''' of the selfish and the tyranny of evil men.
# A [[wrongful]] [[act]].
# [[absence|Absence]] of [[moral]] or [[spiritual]] [[values]], [[lawlessness]].
# [[denial|Denial]] of the [[sovereignty]] of [[God]].

{{rfex}}

